Almost all the best spells are levels 1-3, and as such can be brought to 0% 
fail with every class.  This higher level spells are mostly disappointing.


Fireball, Cone of Cold: Situationally useful, but everything in nethack is 
situationally useful.  Magic Missile is almost always going to be the better 
choice, and the more mana-efficient choice.

Finger of Death: Same effect as the wand.  OK, this is a very powerful 
combat effect.  But all the same, to succeed as a combat caster, one doesn't 
need a level seven spell that costs 35 mana.  All one needs is Magic Missile 
and plenty of XLs.  This is a little like how any class can kick butt in 
melee with +7 Grayswandir, even a class that is restricted at sabre.

Restore Ability: Junk.

Detect Treasure:  If you can cast this reliably, and can afford to spend 
mana on it, you don't need more treasure.

Magic Mapping:  No argument here; this is a good spell.

Create Familiar, Turn Undead, Invisibility: Junk.

Levitation: Terrible levitation source unless you're at least Skilled in 
escape spells.  Even then you're spending 20 or more mana when you could be 
getting it for free from the ring or boots.  Again, everything in nethack is 
situationally useful.  Just like a "D" is a "passing" grade in school.

Teleport Away, Dig: Will save you some wand charges, though it will cost a 
*lot* of mana. These are pretty common wands anyway.

Polymorph: If you can it reliably, you don't need to do more polypiling.

Cancellation:  Not worth the mana against monsters.  For cancelling objects, 
the wand is probably easier to find than the spellbook...



